The '''Skeletal Dragon''' is a unique undead [[Skyrim:Dragon|dragon]] found within [[Skyrim:Labyrinthian|Labyrinthian]] during the quest [[Skyrim:The_Staff_of_Magnus|The Staff of Magnus]]. When killed, it provides a large number of [[Skyrim:Dragon Bone|dragon bones]] but no [[Skyrim:Dragon Scales|dragon scales]], and it will not provide [[Skyrim:Dragon Heartscales|dragon heartscales]] when struck with [[Skyrim:Kahvozein's Fang|Kahvozein's Fang]]. It does not have a dragon soul.

The Skeletal Dragon is an undead creature, and thus is vulnerable to [[SR:Sun Damage|sun damage]]. It also has weakness to  [[Skyrim:Fire Damage|fire damage]]. Unlike other dragons, the skeletal variety doesn't possess blanket immunity to [[Skyrim:Illusion|Illusion]] spells, however the ''[[Skyrim:Master of the Mind|Master of the Mind]]'' perk is required to make Illusion magic effective against it. 
